      "text_unit_id": "tu_0002",
      "verbatim_text": "Angiotensin II receptor blocker neprilysin inhibitor (ARNI)\n-OR-\nAngiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors (ACE inhibitors)\n-OR-\nAngiotensin II receptor blockers (ARBs)\nACE inhibitors and ARBs widen and relax blood vessels and ease the amount of work the heart has to do to pump blood. They also lower blood pressure. ARNIs work similarly but are stronger due to an additional ingredient. To help decide if an ARNI is right for you, the American College of Cardiology has created a tool to help.\nCardioSmart.org/HFDecisionAids\nsacubitril/valsartan (Entresto)\n-OR-\ncaptopril (Capoten)\nenalapril (Vasotec)\nlisinopril (Prinivil, Zestril)\nramipril (Altace)\n-OR-\ncandesartan (Atacand)\nlosartan (Cozaar)\nvalsartan (Diovan)"
    },
